# arb-lab — credential template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored; this file is
# the one tracked exception (.gitignore's `!.env.example`, verified with
# `git check-ignore -v`, which .gitignore:20 insists is the way to check a rule
# actually fires).
#
# NOTHING HERE IS A SECRET. This file holds NAMES ONLY, which is the same rule
# platform/config enforces in the type system: a SecretRef holds a scheme and a
# name (`env:BINANCE_DEMO_API_KEY`), has no field for a value, and an inline
# credential FAILS TO PARSE rather than being politely discouraged. Configs
# reference these variables; only `.env` ever holds the values.
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS SIMULATED MONEY. No mainnet key belongs in this file. When
# one eventually does it is read-only, withdrawals disabled, IP-allowlisted —
# build-spec §7.2's custody policy, not a preference.
#
# DEMO, NOT TESTNET, ON BOTH VENUES. Testnet is a separate deployment whose
# prices, order books and (on Binance) feature set diverge from production;
# demo runs against the production surface. Two consequences that reach the
# spec rather than just convenience:
#   - Binance demo is ONE account with Spot and Futures as tabs, so §4.1's
#     spot!=futures WALLET SPLIT is observable. On testnet those are two
#     unrelated deployments, where the split is not a split — untestable in
#     principle, not merely awkward.
#     BUT NOT THE TRANSFER between them: /sapi/v1/asset/transfer answers an
#     HTML 404 on demo-api.binance.com, i.e. the whole /sapi namespace is
#     ABSENT rather than the endpoint rejecting the request. So §7.1's
#     TransferCollateral path is untestable on demo on BOTH venues — Bybit
#     demo omits transfers by documentation, Binance demo by routing.
#   - Binance's own docs: demo's "IP Limits, Unfilled Order Count, Exchange
#     Filters are EXACTLY the same as the live exchange" (testnet: "generally").
#     So §7.6's rate-limit ladder and #206's LOT-filter question are answerable
#     here with production-identical values.
#
# WHAT DEMO IS NOT FOR: economics. Binance states plainly that "realistic market
# data is not equal to 'real' market data." Milestone 2's kill gate must keep
# using the real unauthenticated capture — demo settles MECHANISM, never carry.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BINANCE — DEMO TRADING (one key, both legs)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mint at https://demo.binance.com/en/my/settings/api-management with all three
# restrictions ticked: Enable Reading, Enable Spot & Margin & Stock Trading,
# Enable Futures. HMAC is fine (Ed25519/RSA also offered). The secret is shown
# ONCE — capture it before leaving the page.
#
#   Spot REST:     https://demo-api.binance.com/api        [doc, verbatim]
#   Spot WS API:   wss://demo-ws-api.binance.com/ws-api/v3 [doc, verbatim]
#   Spot streams:  wss://demo-stream.binance.com/ws  (also :9443, and /stream)
#   Futures REST:  https://demo-fapi.binance.com            [MEASURED, not doc]
#   Futures WS:    wss://demo-fstream.binance.com           [host resolves]
#
# The futures pair is NOT in any doc page reachable from here — the derivatives
# docs answer a fetcher with HTTP 202 and zero bytes (the AWS WAF wall, #180's
# obstacle). demo-fapi was confirmed by probe: /fapi/v1/time returns 200 with a
# serverTime. Treat the WS host as confirmed-resolving but not yet exercised.
#
# Endpoint availability on futures demo, probed unauthenticated (401 = the route
# exists, 404 = it does not): /fapi/v1/leverageBracket, /fapi/v1/positionMargin/
# history, /fapi/v3/positionRisk and /fapi/v2/positionRisk all answer 401;
# /fapi/v1/positionMargin answers "Method GET is invalid", i.e. the path is
# known and POST-only. So #220's live-tier MMR read and #214's act-history
# evidence half are both exercisable here.
BINANCE_DEMO_API_KEY=
BINANCE_DEMO_API_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYBIT — DEMO TRADING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Minted from a MAINNET account switched into Demo Trading mode (avatar -> API).
# Keys made in normal mode will not work, and the docs call using demo keys
# against testnet "meaningless" — the domain must be api-demo.bybit.com.
# Auto-funded: 50,000 USDT, 50,000 USDC, 1 BTC, 1 ETH. No faucet step.
#
#   REST:            https://api-demo.bybit.com
#   Private WS:      wss://stream-demo.bybit.com
#   Public WS/REST:  MAINNET (wss://stream.bybit.com) — demo has no public feed
#                    of its own, which is what §3.4's mark class wants:
#                    production mark movement against a simulated position.
#
# Known gaps (bybit-exchange.github.io/docs/v5/demo): no asset-transfer or
# withdrawal endpoints, no WS Trade, orders retained 7 days, default rate limit
# not upgradable. §7.1's TransferCollateral path therefore cannot be exercised
# here — that is the only thing the testnet pair below is for.
BYBIT_DEMO_API_KEY=
BYBIT_DEMO_API_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYBIT — TESTNET (optional; only for the transfer path demo cannot serve)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   REST:  https://api-testnet.bybit.com
#   WS:    wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com
#
# Leave blank until §7.1's TransferCollateral slice needs it.
BYBIT_TESTNET_API_KEY=
BYBIT_TESTNET_API_SECRET=
